<section class="hub-group" aria-label="Read"><h2 class="hub-group-t">Read</h2><ul class="hub-grid"><li><a class="hub-card" href="/profiles"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">460 profiles</span><span class="hub-card-t">Profiles</span><span class="hub-card-d">In-depth histories of states and empires, religions and languages: their origins, great ages and legacies, with key facts and timelines.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/encyclopedia/"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/library-of-alexandria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">32,011 entries</span><span class="hub-card-t">Encyclopedia</span><span class="hub-card-d">People, places, events, institutions and ideas, with 22,549 historical pictures.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/state/"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">5,468 states</span><span class="hub-card-t">States</span><span class="hub-card-d">Every recorded kingdom, principality, republic and chiefdom, with its lineage and connections.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/countries/"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-wall-of-china.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">190 countries</span><span class="hub-card-t">Country Histories</span><span class="hub-card-d">The history of each present-day country, told through the states that lay on its soil.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/people/"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/las-meninas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">12,935 people</span><span class="hub-card-t">People</span><span class="hub-card-d">Rulers, thinkers, artists and explorers, century by century and region by region, with a chart of who lived when.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/speeches/"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pericles.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">80 speeches</span><span class="hub-card-t">Great Speeches</span><span class="hub-card-d">The words that moved history: the setting, the key passage, what followed, and the complete text where it is free to read.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/today-in-history/"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mesoamerican-long-count-calendar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">3,122 events</span><span class="hub-card-t">Today in History</span><span class="hub-card-d">What happened on each day of the year, across five thousand years.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/encyclopedia/glossary"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/code-of-hammurabi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">723 terms</span><span class="hub-card-t">Glossary</span><span class="hub-card-d">Offices, institutions, laws and ideas of the past, each explained in a sentence.</span></span></a></li></ul></section><section class="hub-group" aria-label="Through time"><h2 class="hub-group-t">Through time</h2><ul class="hub-grid hub-5"><li><a class="hub-card" href="/atlas"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/catalan-atlas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">From 3500 BCE to today</span><span class="hub-card-t">Atlas</span><span class="hub-card-d">The world in any year: slide through five thousand years and watch states appear and vanish.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/timeline"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/standard-of-ur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">Every state</span><span class="hub-card-t">World Timeline</span><span class="hub-card-d">Five thousand years of states and empires on one line, region by region: see who lived alongside whom.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/faiths"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/borobudur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">18 religions</span><span class="hub-card-t">Faith Maps</span><span class="hub-card-d">Where each religion began, how it spread and where it last lived on, century by century on a turning globe.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/centuries/"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bayeux-tapestry.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">51 centuries</span><span class="hub-card-t">Centuries</span><span class="hub-card-d">World history one century at a time: the great powers, key events, people and a map.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/years/"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">1,027 years</span><span class="hub-card-t">Year by Year</span><span class="hub-card-d">What happened in a single year: its events, the people born and the people who died, the states founded and ended.</span></span></a></li></ul></section><section class="hub-group" aria-label="Explore"><h2 class="hub-group-t">Explore</h2><ul class="hub-grid hub-6"><li><a class="hub-card" href="/explorer"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trajans-column.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">Power curves</span><span class="hub-card-t">Empire Explorer</span><span class="hub-card-d">Compare the rise and fall of nearly four hundred states and empires on one timeline.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/race"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charioteer-of-delphi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">426 to race</span><span class="hub-card-t">Rise and Fall Race</span><span class="hub-card-d">Up to four states and empires race year by year: who led, when they overtook each other and how long each held on.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/connections"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">11,296 links</span><span class="hub-card-t">Connections</span><span class="hub-card-d">Who succeeded, conquered, ruled or merged with whom: the states as one network.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/paths/"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marco-polo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">38 paths</span><span class="hub-card-t">Reading Paths</span><span class="hub-card-d">Themed routes across profiles and entries, from the Silk Road to the steppe empires.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/write"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rosetta-stone.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">12 languages</span><span class="hub-card-t">Write in Ancient Scripts</span><span class="hub-card-d">Cuneiform, hieroglyphs, Linear B, runes, Brahmi and more: a keyboard that shows every sign with its sound, and your writing as a picture.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/start"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tabula-rogeriana.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">Four questions</span><span class="hub-card-t">Find Your Way In</span><span class="hub-card-d">Tell us what draws you to history and get the reading paths and tools that suit you.</span></span></a></li></ul></section><section class="hub-group" aria-label="Play"><h2 class="hub-group-t">Play</h2><ul class="hub-grid hub-5"><li><a class="hub-card" href="/quiz"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rosetta-stone.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">New every day</span><span class="hub-card-t">History Quiz</span><span class="hub-card-d">Guess the empire, person, event or place from four clues, or practise as long as you like.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/games"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pythian-games.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">Nine games</span><span class="hub-card-t">Games</span><span class="hub-card-d">Picture puzzles, word hunts, timelines, a globe, a daily Connections and a daily Crossword: games with real pictures and real dates, for every age.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/flashcards"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-wisdom.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">5,459 cards</span><span class="hub-card-t">Flashcards</span><span class="hub-card-d">Terms, faces, capitals and dates in decks of cards: the ones you miss come back sooner, the ones you know wait longer.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/kids"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-pyramid-of-giza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">For young explorers</span><span class="hub-card-t">Kids corner</span><span class="hub-card-d">Pyramids, knights, Vikings and explorers: picture stories, a fact of the day and games for younger readers.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/passport"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xuanzang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">Your stamps</span><span class="hub-card-t">My Passport</span><span class="hub-card-d">The pages you read, the centuries you visit and the games you play, with stamps to collect. Kept in your own browser.</span></span></a></li></ul></section><section class="hub-group" aria-label="The Institute"><h2 class="hub-group-t">The Institute</h2><ul class="hub-grid hub-5"><li><a class="hub-card" href="/research-series"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thucydides.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">5 essays</span><span class="hub-card-t">Research Series</span><span class="hub-card-d">Thematic essays on the forces behind the rise and collapse of civilisations.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/teachers/"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-amos-comenius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">68 worksheets</span><span class="hub-card-t">Teachers' Corner</span><span class="hub-card-d">Printable worksheets with answer keys on the reading paths and the centuries, and ideas for teaching with the site.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/dataset"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhind-mathematical-papyrus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">CC BY 4.0</span><span class="hub-card-t">Open Data</span><span class="hub-card-d">The states register (5,468 states, 11,296 relations) and the power curves, free to reuse.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/community"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/althing.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">Readers and writers</span><span class="hub-card-t">Community</span><span class="hub-card-d">Essays and opinions from the Institute's readers, and a place to share your own.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="hub-card" href="/contributors"><span class="hub-card-img"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/book-of-kells.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><span class="hub-card-b"><span class="hub-card-k">Contribute</span><span class="hub-card-t">Write for Us</span><span class="hub-card-d">Research, write or check facts with the Institute: three ways to take part.</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
